Package: researchreproducibility
Title: Reproducibility Audits of Research Projects and Articles
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Audits the conditions for reproducing research. For a project
    directory, checks documentation, licence, citation metadata, declared
    and pinned dependencies, containers, pipelines, continuous integration,
    data availability and documentation, absolute paths, random seeds and
    large files, each with its evidence and the standard it comes from. For
    an article, detects data and code availability, availability
    statements, preregistration and shared materials in the full text with
    explicit, versioned rules; a text that cannot be read is unverifiable,
    never "no". Writes HTML and JSON reports, creates reproducible project
    skeletons and a GitHub Actions workflow that runs the audit.
